{"symbol":"VOYA","area":"sp500","updated":"2026-11-09T19:39:56Z","info":{"address1":"200 Park Avenue","city":"New York","state":"NY","zip":"10166","country":"United States","phone":"212 309 8200","website":"https://www.voya.com","industry":"Financial Conglomerates","industryKey":"financial-conglomerates","industryDisp":"Financial Conglomerates","sector":"Financial Services","sectorKey":"financial-services","sectorDisp":"Financial Services","longBusinessSummary":"Voya Financial, Inc. provides workplace benefits, and savings solutions and technologies in the United States and internationally. The company operates through three segments: Retirement, Investment Management and Employee Benefits. The Retirement segment offers full-service retirement products; recordkeeping services; stable value and fixed general account investment products; non-qualified plan administration services; and tools, guidance, and services to promote the financial well-being and retirement security of employees. This segment also provides wealth management services, such as individual retirement, managed, and brokerage accounts, as well as financial guidance and advisory services. This segment serves corporate, public and private school systems, higher education institutions, hospitals and healthcare facilities, other non-profit organizations, and state and local governments, as well as institutional clients and individual customers. The Employee Benefits segment offers various insurance products comprising stop loss, group life, group disability, whole and term life, critical illness, accident, and hospital indemnity insurance. This segment also provides worksite employee benefits, health account solutions, leave management, benefits administration, health plan enrollment, financial wellness, and decision support products and services to mid-size and large corporate employers and professional associations. The Investment Management segment provides fixed income, equity, multi-asset, and alternative products and solutions to individual investors, financial intermediaries, and institutional clients through its direct sales force, consultant channel, intermediary partners, banks, broker-dealers, and independent financial advisers. The company was formerly known as ING U.S., Inc. and changed its name to Voya Financial, Inc. in April 2014. Voya Financial, Inc. was founded in 1975 and is based in New York, New York.","fullTimeEmployees":11000,"companyOfficers":[{"maxAge":1,"name":"Ms. Heather Hamilton Lavallee","age":55,"title":"President, CEO & Director","yearBorn":1970,"fiscalYear":2025,"totalPay":5518925,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Mr. Michael Robert Katz","age":49,"title":"Executive VP & CFO","yearBorn":1976,"fiscalYear":2025,"totalPay":4114450,"exercisedValue":1545000,"unexercisedValue":870458},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Mr. Santhosh Iyengar Keshavan","age":51,"title":"Executive VP and Chief Technology & Operations Officer","yearBorn":1974,"fiscalYear":2025,"totalPay":3065460,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":870458},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Mr. Matthew  Toms C.F.A.","age":52,"title":"Chief Executive Officer of Voya Investment Management","yearBorn":1973,"fiscalYear":2025,"totalPay":4474039,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Mr. Jay Stuart Kaduson","age":49,"title":"Chief Executive Officer of Workplace Solutions","yearBorn":1976,"fiscalYear":2025,"totalPay":3977084,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Mr. Tony Donghui Oh","title":"Chief Accounting Officer & Corporate Controller","fiscalYear":2025,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Mr. Trevor  Ogle","age":48,"title":"Executive VP & Chief Legal Officer","yearBorn":1977,"fiscalYear":2025,"exercisedValue":0,"unexercisedValue":0},{"maxAge":1,"name":"Mr. Mark A. Sides","title":"Chair, SVP, Chief Compliance Officer and Deputy General Counsel of Government Affairs & Ethics","fiscalYear":2025,"exercisedValue":0,"u